WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>Southmost
Point of
Shizuoka</b>

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.990
Oh, Omaezaki, here, at this precipice, the sea is split into two: 
the light of Suruga and the wind of Tohtoumi.
-Maruyama Kaoru

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.290
<i>It's the ocean!</i>

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.220
<i>But... I have to resist acting like that.</i>

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.030
<i>The water's so nice.</i>

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:39.970
<i>What a pretty view.</i>

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.090
<i>I took nearly fifty photos of 
the ocean on the way here.</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.360
<i>Such is a resident of a landlocked prefecture.</i>

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.540
<i>There are pawprints on the steps.</i>

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>Power doggy.</i>

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.600
<i>Next, I have to go to the tea shop in 
Kakegawa that Mom wanted me to visit.</i>

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.030
<i>I've put together a perfect 
itinerary this time.</i>

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.060
<i>I won't make any mistakes like last time...</i>

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.100
<i>I think.</i>

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.780
<i>Riding by the ocean feels great!</i>

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.980
<i>But...</i>

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.080
<i>It's so windy and cold!</i>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:16.710
<b>(2) Episode 2 
New Year's Solo Camper Girl</b>

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.220
<i>Tea...</i>

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.030
<i>There are too many kinds.</i>

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.140
<i>I don't know which ones are good.</i>

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.060
Excuse me.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.040
Do you have any teas that you could 
recommend for around 2,000 yen?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.760
Let's see...

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.320
How about this Himekura here?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.900
It's aged in a shed in the 
mountains over the summer.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.120
It has an especially soft 
flavor that goes down easy.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.980
<i>I don't know what she's 
talking about, but it's tasty.</i>

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.050
Wait...

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.950
Might you be the young lady 
I met at Yashajin Pass?

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.870
Oh, right!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.070
Hello.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:57.400
Thank you for the houjicha tea.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.850
It was delicious.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:03:59.880
You're welcome.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.910
What a coincidence, huh?

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.640
Are you here in Kakegawa by yourself today?

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.510
Yes.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.340
I'm going to see the first sunrise of 
the new year over the ocean in Iwata.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.410
Ah, so that's what brought you all 
the way out here from Yamanashi.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.750
If you're going to Iwata, 
you might enjoy Fukude Beach.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.900
Fukude Beach?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.820
Yes.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.900
It's a famous spot for the New Year's sunrise.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.910
<b>Fukude Beach</b>

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.910
Omaezaki
Enshunada

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.910
Waves can reach 2.9 meters.
Evacuate immediately in the event 
of an earthquake or tsunami!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.910
No Swimming

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.910
They put up a torii at the end of the year,

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.160
which gives it a bit of a mysterious vibe.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.280
I'll check it out, then.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.720
Well, take care.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.220
Visit us again sometime.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.170
Sure.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.950
I just bought tea at the shop.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.420
Thanks!

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.770
There's a green tea café on 
the second floor of the shop.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.320
You should take a break there.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.600
I gave you an extra 1,000 yen.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.310
Really?!

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.220
My, you're back already?

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.940
H-Hi...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.120
<i>It's an actual café.</i>

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.550
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.720
Here's your matcha tiramisu 
and green tea set.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.830
Well, let's try it out.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.010
<i>How is this tea set so relaxing?</i>

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.960
<i>Reminds me of the hot spring in Komagane.</i>

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.470
<i>It's like a warm bath, but in drink form.</i>

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.970
<i>Shoot, I don't feel like moving anymore.</i>

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.340
<i>I just want to pitch my tent here.</i>

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.850
That's it for the lower half!

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:46.580
Those are some really dark clouds...

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.380
<i>And here we are at Mitsuke-Tenjin Shrine.</i>

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.700
<i>Right on schedule.</i>

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.360
<i>I'm glad I timed my stops 
and travel times so well.</i>

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.890
<i>So this is Shippeitarou...</i>

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.040
<i>It looks a little more fox-like 
than Hayatarou over at Kouzenji.</i>

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.770
<i>It sure is quiet on New Year's Eve.</i>

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.150
<b>Wishing Cow
(Female)
</b>Touch it to make a wish

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.490
<i>It's a cow.</i>

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.900
<i>I guess I'll call this my New Year's visit.</i>

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:31.700
<i>I wish for another peaceful year.</i>

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:33.350
<i>Now...</i>

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.450
<i>I gotta go check out the 
real-life Shippeitarou!</i>

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.170
Um...

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.420
<b>Shippei
Charms 
and 
Fortunes</b>

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:43.980
I heard Shippeitarou the Third lives here.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.910
Unfortunately, a few years ago...

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.430
<b>Tarou's Grave</b>

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.910
<i>Come to think of it, dogs only 
live for about fifteen years.</i>

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.510
<i>Not nearly as long as humans.</i>

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:06.480
I came to see Shippei the Third at 
Mitsuke-Tenjin, but he's already passed on.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.700
Oh, that's too bad.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.950
It got me thinking...

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.450
Dogs have much shorter lives than humans.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.200
You can't be together for decades.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:23.210
Don't you ever get scared about 
Chikuwa leaving you, Saitou?

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.480
It is really scary, and I'll be
 really sad when it happens...

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.740
But it's inevitable.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:36.480
That's why I want to play with him lots,
so he can remember all the fun he had.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.220
I see.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.450
Speaking of, ever since 
our Christmas camping trip,

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:45.340
Chikuwa gets really excited when 
he sees photos of you guys.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.150
Oh, really?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.740
Come play with me again, Rin-chan!

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.740
All right, I'll play with you 
so much, you'll go nuts.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.740
<b>Talismans & Charms</b>

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.740
<b>Prayers</b>

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.260
Thank you.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.530
<i>Shippeitarou doggy charm acquired.</i>

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.750
<i>I should head to the campground.</i>

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.080
<i>Hey, good luck.</i>

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.670
One night at the free sites, correct?

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.260
Yes.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.000
<i>The ocean's just past there, huh?</i>

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.460
<i>Gotta set up quick!</i>

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.160
<i>All right, let's go check out the ocean!</i>

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:31.650
<b>B A T H S</b>

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.980
<i>There's a lighthouse here, too.</i>

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.600
<i>Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.670
<i>It's small, but you can definitely 
see it from here, too.</i>

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.690
<i>The sun's setting.</i>

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.190
<i>I should start my campfire.</i>

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.950
<i>There are no pine cones or twigs in a 
well-maintained campground, though,</i>

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.450
<i>so I'm going to start my 
fire with a feather stick.</i>

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:26.710
Feather Stick

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:24.730
<i>A feather stick is a piece of 
firewood shaved into thin strips</i>

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.460
<i>with a knife to use as tinder.</i>

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.190
<i>That should do it.</i>

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:31.780
<i>Now to boil some water with my burner...</i>

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.970
<i>It kind of looks like a spider lily.</i>

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:43.580
<i>I won't need firestarters anymore
 if this works so well.</i>

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.730
<i>Farewell, pine cones.</i>

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.170
Yo, wait up!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.470
Yo, wait up!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.350
<i>Okay, it's boiling.</i>

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.150
<i>I'll make some simple 
New Year's soba with this.</i>

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.480
<b>Duck Soup Soba</b>

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:55.990
<i>Boil some nameko mushrooms 
along with the soba,</i>

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.630
<i>then top it with green onions, 
seaweed, deep-fried fish, and egg.</i>

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.490
<i>Give it a good shake of shichimi pepper, and...</i>

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.130
<i>Duck soup nameko mushroom soba.</i>

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.380
<i>Just putting it in a bowl really 
sets the mood for New Year's Eve.</i>

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.000
Time to eat.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.440
<i>You can't go winter camping 
without spicy soup.</i>

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:31.990
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:34.020
<i>I forgot to post my photos.</i>

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.910
I uploaded my New Year's
 solo camping photos.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:40.280
Wow! It's the ocean!

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.130
You took way too many pictures 
of the ocean, Rin-chan.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:44.280
<i>That was fast.</i>

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.520
Yamanashi kids can never get enough 
of the ocean, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:49.550
Exactly.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.610
You take tons of pictures of 
Mt. Fuji yourself, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.290
You got me there!

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.340
Happy New Year!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.250
Not just yet.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.050
You can give me a Namazon gift card
 instead of money this year!

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.520
I'll send you a 20,000 yen one. Used.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:08.110
Hey, by the way, it's snowing over here! Snow!

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.110
Really?

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.600
It never snows in Hamamatsu.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.690
It's so exciting!

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.700
<i>The latter half of the year 
was pretty noisy thanks to her.</i>

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.640
<i>I normally only camp until January,</i>

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.350
<i>but I have a feeling I'm going to be camping 
even when it gets warm next year.</i>

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.290
<i>I have my license now, too.</i>

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.460
Happy New Year, Rin-chan!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.460
Happy New Year.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.940
'Sup, Inuko?

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.770
HNY.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:59.700
Happy New Year.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.700
Sure is cold, huh?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.750
HNY, Sensei.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.040
Happy New Year, Ohgaki-san.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:09.410
Man, thanks for offering to drive us.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.710
It's fine. I didn't have any plans.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.460
Aki, are you going to see the first 
sunrise before you go to work?

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:17.440
Yeah.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.520
Are you going to Takayama after this, Inuko?

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.960
In the afternoon.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.470
Snowball

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:24.340
Aki-chan!

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.290
HNY!

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.580
M-Mini Inuko!

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.650
I told her we're going to see the first 
sunrise, and she wanted to tag along.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.810
Aki-chan, can I have a New Year's allowance?

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.890
Aoi-chan told me you work lots.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.530
<i>This kid...</i>

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:48.280
<i>Here we are at Fukude Beach.</i>

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.760
<i>It's already pretty crowded.</i>

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:06.260
Welcoming the New Year

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:03.980
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.260
<i>There's the torii in the middle 
of nowhere on the beach.</i>

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.740
<i>She was right.</i>

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:10.820
<i>It's kind of mysterious.</i>

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.520
<b>Mt. Minobu Ropeway</b>

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.520
It's cold! Super cold!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.580
It must be even colder on the mountaintop.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:20.180
I don't think I've seen the 
New Year's sunrise in years.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.530
Now that you mention it, I haven't, either.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:40.730
It's so pretty, Aoi-chan.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:41.550
Sure is.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.920
The shops are open and everything.

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.570
Aki-chan, buy me dango!

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.260
Buy your own.

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.820
One yomogi, please.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:55.350
I'll have a yuba, then.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:58.100
We cut the skewers for good luck.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.360
<b>Kushi-Kiri Dango
</b>Cut the skewer (kushi) 
to cut off suffering and death (kushi)<b></b>

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.450
Cutting the skewers to cut off 
suffering and death, huh?

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:05.860
That's so punny.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.780
Yomogi

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.780
Yuba

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.780
<b>Shine</b>

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.620
You're going to eat <i>two</i>?

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.870
They're handing out amazake over there.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.380
Minobu Ropeway

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.510
We have some time until sunrise.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.610
Why don't we go visit the shrine first?

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.910
Okay!

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.850
I guess New Year's greeting card 
deliveries will be starting soon, huh?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.130
Yeah.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.390
Happy New Year.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.390
Thank you.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:42.760
Next is...

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.000
Fujita-san!

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.910
I wish for Aki-chan to give me 
a big New Year's allowance.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:55.410
<b>Monday, January 1st</b>

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.410
Ten more minutes until sunrise.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:56.910
Almost time.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.590
Rin must be waiting for the sunrise
at the beach about now.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.450
<b>100 Famous Mountains of Yamanashi 
Mt. Minobu Summit
Altitude: 1153m</b>

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.340
Here it comes.

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:23.940
Yeah.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.050
Here it comes.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.450
Welcoming the New Year

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:06.680
HNY.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.160
HNY!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.990
It's a double New Year's sunrise.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.130
All right.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:22.700
Gotta keep up the pace on 
my greeting card deliveries!

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.870
Thanks for the New Year's sunrises.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.030
I'm looking forward to 
another year with you all.

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:32.250
<i>Well, guess I'll head back to the campground.</i>

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:42.520
<b>Happy New Year</b>

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:42.520
<b>Beach Road 
Development Group</b>

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.990
<i>They're tossing rice cakes.</i>

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:52.730
It's so pretty.

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.210
Come on, let's go.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:03.050
We should get moving before the New Year's 
visitors arrive and cause a traffic jam.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.360
Besides, we need to go check out 
the next New Year's sunrise.

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:09.660
The next one?

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:15.240
<i>I got more than I expected.</i>

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:22.580
<i>I guess I'll burn the rest of my firewood 
and relax with a book until checkout.</i>

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.900
<i>And for lunch,</i>

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:29.810
<b>Iwata's Local Specialty Curry</b>

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:29.810
<b>Creamy Pig's Foot Curry</b>

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:29.310
<i>I'll have the famous pig's foot curry 
before I make my way home.</i>

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:36.570
<i>I smell something savory...</i>

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.950
Pizza for sale!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.550
Care for some pizza?

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:42.450
<i>A pizza truck?</i>

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:46.210
<b>Margherita Pizza w/ lots of cheese
Small: 800 yen
Half: 450 yen</b>

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:46.210
<b>Pot-au-Feu
350 yen</b>

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.980
<i>Margherita and pot-au-feu...</i>

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:49.550
<i>No, no!</i>

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.680
<i>I can't fill up now!</i>

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.210
<i>Fight the pizza, Rin!</i>

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:59.720
<b>Iwata's Local Specialty Curry

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:59.720
<i>The hungrier I am,
 the better the curry will be!</i>

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:02.520
<i>Okay.</i>

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:03.830
<i>Don't do it. Don't give in.</i>

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.440
<i>She gave in.</i>

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.930
The pot-au-feu is so good, too.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.240
I see.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.570
Diamond Fuji, huh?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.240
<i>"Diamond Fuji."</i>

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:25.620
Diamond Fuji
An optical phenomenon in which the rising sun
 is obscured by the peak of Mt. Fuji, 
resulting in a diamond-like flare.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.740
<i>So called for its diamond-like appearance,</i>

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:25.020
<i>it refers to the sun rising behind
the volcanic peak of Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:32.200
<i>And because of Mt. Fuji's height, 
the sunrise occurs later than usual.</i>

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.170
Sunrise at Mt. Minobu was at seven.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:40.130
Diamond Fuji will be visible from 
Takaori in Fujikawa City at 7:50.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:45.120
And we're traveling in the meantime 
so that we can see the sunrise twice, right?

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.020
That's so cool!

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.240
Good thinking, Aki-chan.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.820
This is going to be quite the mountain road.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.500
Ohgaki-san, how are we for time?

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.090
Three more minutes.

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:00.280
Are we going to make it?

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:02.370
You can do it, Sensei!

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.460
I suppose so.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.290
I'll get us there in time!

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.400
Sensei, it's just around that corner!

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.230
I see it!

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:53.600
The Diamond Fuji New Year's sunrise!

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.330
It's... way up there already.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:02.470
Oh.

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:07.640
The Diamond Fuji sunrise was at 7:20.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.720
Whoopsie!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.460
The first sunrise...

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:43.530
HNY!

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.720
I got a picture of the first sunrise.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:48.070
Hey, you're finally awake.

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:49.030
HNY.

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.230
<b>Mom</b>

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:53.500
It's Mom.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:55.950
Hello?

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.160
<i>Happy New Year, Rin.</i>

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:00.540
Yeah. Happy New Year.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.040
<i>Is it warm enough over there?</i>

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.240
It's way warmer than Minobu.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:04.990
What's up?

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.230
<i>You said you're coming home today, right?</i>

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:10.010
Yeah, you said Grandpa was coming.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:12.510
<i>Well, about that... It snowed over here.</i>

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:13.750
So I heard.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.110
<i>All the roads are frozen.</i>

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.000
<i>You won't make it home on your moped.</i>

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.690
<i>It doesn't look like it's 
going to thaw any time soon.</i>

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:23.240
Seriously?

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:26.360
<i>I talked to your grandpa about it,</i>

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:31.390
<i>and he said he'll come get you and your 
moped the day after tomorrow in his van.</i>

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.100
Really?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:37.370
<i>So just enjoy your time there
until the morning of the third.</i>

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:43.800
The third, huh?

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:47.690
Now I have two full days to waste.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:50.900
What should I do?

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:35.240
Next Episode

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:35.240
<b>Surprise Camping and Some Deep Thoughts</b>

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:39.960
When camping...

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:39.960
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:39.960
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:39.960
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!
